CUDA streams allow asynchronous operations. By using multiple streams, you can overlap a kernel on one chunk of data while transferring the next chunk:

```cpp
for (int i = 0; i < N; i += chunk) {
    cudaMemcpyAsync(d_in + i, h_in + i, chunk_size, cudaMemcpyHostToDevice, stream[i]);
    kernel<<<grid, block, 0, stream[i]>>>(d_in + i, d_out + i);
    cudaMemcpyAsync(h_out + i, d_out + i, chunk_size, cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost, stream[i]);
}
```

This creates a pipeline where transfer and compute overlap, hiding PCIe latency.
